              "blocks": {
                "text_Hx4yEx": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Finding the right lab-grown diamond engagement ring comes down to a few important considerations:<br/><br/><strong>Understand the Four Cs. </strong><br/>Cut, color, clarity, and carat weight are the primary characteristics that determine a diamond's beauty and value. Of these, cut has the greatest impact on brilliance and sparkle.<br/><br/><strong>Set a budget. </strong><br/>Lab-grown diamond engagement rings typically cost 40% less than comparable mined-diamond rings, which means your budget goes further — whether that means a larger stone, a more intricate setting, or both.<br/><br/><strong>Know your partner's style. </strong><br/>Pay attention to the jewelry they already wear. Do they gravitate toward classic pieces, vintage designs, or modern minimalism? If you're unsure, MiaDonna's non-commissioned jewelry experts offer free consultations to help you decide.<br/><br/><strong>Choose the right metal. </strong><br/>Consider your partner's skin tone, lifestyle, and existing jewelry when selecting between platinum, white gold, yellow gold, or rose gold.<br/><br/><strong>Think about lifestyle. </strong><br/>An active partner may prefer a lower-profile setting like a bezel or flush mount, while someone who loves glamour may prefer a halo or side-stone design.<br/><br/><strong>Verify ring size. </strong><br/>Use MiaDonna's Ring Sizing Guide or borrow a ring your partner already wears on their ring finger. Every MiaDonna engagement ring includes one complimentary resizing within 60 days.<br/><br/><strong>Look for certification. </strong><br/>MiaDonna lab-grown diamonds are certified by recognized grading organizations, ensuring verified quality and authenticity.</p>",
